  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value rose 2.4% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $16.19B (2.4% higher over 30D) shows tokenization still adding balance sheet\u2014consistent with Institutions building exposure through treasury, credit, or fund wrappers rather than pausing after prior growth. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/neuberger-launches-tokenized-fixed-income-fund-with-securitize?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Neuberger teams with Securitize on multi-chain tokenized fixed-income fund launch</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows.</li><li><strong>Tokenized T-bill supply is still expanding through new products:</strong> That usually shows up first as new issuer and product supply, then as higher distributed value and denser collateral-style use across networks and platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-08-18-securitize-neubergers-230-billion-fixed-income-platform-onchain-new-tokenized-fund-412102\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Securitize brings Neuberger\u2019s $230 billion fixed-income platform onchain with new tokenized fund</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-08-18-blockchain-association-backs-secs-proposal-to-scrap-outdated-nms-rules-citing-tokenization-benefits-412069\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Blockchain Association backs SEC\u2019s proposal to scrap outdated NMS rules, citing tokenization benefits</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
